t always*               displaying or setting the insertion point correctly.** Version 2.0d5  February 10, 1988     Harry Yee & Steve Glass*   The procedure PrintCheck and its corresponding routines	have been commented	out*   because none of	this code was really being used and it caused problems while*   printing to a spooler.** Version 2.0d6  March 1, 1988         Suki Lee & Steve Glass*   Bug fix: Move the code to initialize the port and to reset the printer from *   LLDText to LLDStartUp. Deleted the same code from InitPrinting (called at the*   beginning of LLDBitMap). Now the port is initialized only once at startup time *   and not each time LLDText and LLDBitMap is called.*   Commented out CheckPrinter routine since it is not being called by anyone.*   Also commented out InitSSC and replaced calls to it with calls to ResetPrinter*   since the two functions similarly.*   The escapes codes for resetting the	printer has been modified to used the *   default character, Elite, rather than Pica since the printer is optimized to *   print in Elite.** Version 2.0d7   March 25, 1988	Suki Lee*   Bug fix: added	filtering of c cedilla in LLDText so the character will be*   printed in draft mode.*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------** Version 2.1d2   May 5, 1988        Suki Lee*   Bug fix: *   - Added code to	check status of AppleTalk connected printer. Puts up*     appropriate message to warn user of condition.*   - LQ no longer ejects an extra page	for each page printed.* Version 2.1d3   May 9, 1988        Suki Lee*   Bug fix: *   - Added code to	ask the printer for	an ID which indicates if a color ribbon*     is installed.	If printing to an ImageWriter I or if no color ribbon is *     installed, the color selection on	the job dialog is overridden. The routine*     CheckPrinter which was removed in	2.0d6 has been modified and added back.** Version 2.1d4   June 8, 1988       Suki Lee*   Bug fix:*   - Added error checking for opening connection to device.** Version 2.1d5   June 24, 1988      Suki Lee*   Bug fix:*   - Took out branch for background printing in LLDStartup	which doesn't clean *     up the stack properly.*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------** Version 2.2d1   July 25, 1988      Suki Lee*   Bug fix:*   - Added a flag to indicate when not	to display status message, as in the case *     of PrPixelMap	where the dialog box is not put up.** Version 2.2d2   July 26, 1988      Suki Lee*   Bug fix:*   - When printing	in Better Text mode, some color text were not printed when*     color is not selected, no color ribbon is installed in an ImageWriter II,*     or printing to an ImageWriter I. Fixed the logic in MakePattern, which *     calculates the dot pattern for color mapping, so the correct branch is taken*     for 640 mode high resolution. Also changed the names of some of the branch*     labels for clarity.** Version 2.2d3   August 5, 1988     Suki Lee*   Bug fix:*   - AppleTalk will not return from a synchronous write if	something happened to *     the device while the write is in progress. This poses	a problem for error *     conditions such as out of paper for an AppleTalk connected ImageWriter. As *     per Greg Seitz, recovery is possible if asynchronous writes are used. This *     change is made in the subroutine PrDevWrite. Also rewrote the loop logic in *     this routine because it was wasteful.*   - Use GetCursorAd before the WaitCursor call and use SetCursor instead of*     InitCursor when done to restore the original cursor.**-------------------------------------------------------------------------------* Version 3.0* d1 November 28, 1988     Suki Lee*    Two new calls are added: PrGetPrinterSpecs, which returns the printer's  *    type and its characteristics (only	color capability is	defined for now) and*    PrGetPageOrientation which returns	either portrait or landscape.These calls*    are needed by IIGS HyperCard printing.*   * d2 December 15, 1988    Suki Lee*    Added new header to denote this as	a driver which support the new calls *    PrGetPrinterSpecs and PrGetPgOrientation (and any subsequent new calls).*    This header is	2 words long: first	word is 0 followed by a call count word.*     *    Fixed the jump	to an incorrect exit routine in PrPixelmap if unsafe to *    proceed. The correct routine is Exit10, not Exit8.* * d3 January 19, 1989     Suki Lee*    Added a new input parameter, handle to the print record, to PrGetPgOrientation.**    January 24, 1989     Suki Lee*    Modified PrGetPgOrientation to use	Exit4 instead of Exit0 since a long parameter*    has been added.** d4 Februray 6,1989      Suki Lee*    Modified PrValidate so that it will no longer call CiXMetrics if the print	record*    is valid for the printer type and is the correct version. This was not necessary*    and caused problems for applications that want to modify fields in the record such*    as the page rectangle. **    February 8, 1989     Suki Lee*    Added in code in PrPicFile to check the size of Quick Draw's buffer if Better Text*    is requested. If the buffer is too small, we grow the buffer to what we need and *    restore it back to the original size.**    February 10, 1989    Suki Lee*    Bug fix in PrValidate: the print record handle is now dereferenced before using.** d5 February 23, 1989    Suki Lee*    Further bug fix in PrValidate: PtrToHand call is changed to BlockMove since the *    print record handle has been deferenced. An error was being returned from the*    PtrToHand call, causing the code to display the dialogs to be skipped.** d6 March 8, 1989        Suki Lee*    Added code in PrValidate to copy the print record into the local data stroage area *    since the driver code works off the local copy of the print record.* *    Modified status display code to use LETextBox2 instead of DrawString, so text will*    be wrapped, especially for 320 mode.**    March 9, 1989        Suki Lee*    Modified PrPicFile to use rPage data from PrInfo subrecord instead of PrInfoPt. *    The application may modify rPage between pages and since PrInfoPt is designated *    as reserved in the reference manual, the data there may not be accurate.**    Added constant values for iHRes and iVRes in landscape mode. Added code to modify*    these values based on page orientation in CiXmetrics.**    March 14, 1989       Suki Lee*    Added initialization of two variables: ZeroPage and SCBValue in PrValidate. This is *    a measure to safeguard against cases where the application enters the print loop *    without calling PrDefault, PrStlDialog or PrJobDialog, where these variables are *    currently being initialized.*    * d7 March 29, 1989       Suki Lee*    Modified band buffer allocation code to find MaxBlock and if it is larger than 64K,*    we use 64K, else we use the maxblock size. This created a minor problem where an *    entire 8 1/2 x 11 page can fit inside of one band and the idleproc which checks for*    cancel is called each band in the high level routines. A new routine LLDIdleProc is *    implemented so the idleproc can be called from the low level routines, taking care *    of D page swapping and proper stack clean up. This new routine also allows for *    cancelling of printing if there is a printer error.** d8 April 11, 1989       Suki Lee*    Added error checking in status calls. If status returns error indicating printer is*    not available (e.g. turned off), then we avoid any further reads or writes. BRC # *    47474-47478.** d9 April 25, 1989       Suki Lee*    Modified InsertPaperAlert to display arrow cursor instead of restoring the cursor*    set by the application, since some applications set the watch cursor before entering*    the print loop.*   *    Bug fix: Idleproc pointer in the print record is not set up correctly with the *    defalut idle proc in draft mode. Added set up code in PrOpenDoc and PrPixelMap.** d10 May 2, 1989         Suki Lee*    Revert PrValidate to recalculating the whole print record each time, so applications can *    modifiy one field and have the rest of the record be consistent. Change code in PrOpenDoc*    to just look at the type and version field of the print record instead of calling *    PrValidate. This is needed for Iduna printing.* *    Bug fix: Added error checking code so that draft and PrPixelMap printing can use the*    LLDIdleProc to cancel out print job. BRC #48936** d11 May 19, 1989         Suki Lee*    Landscape prints garbage if the buffer size is larger than the standard size. Added code *    to use only standard buffer if landscape is selected. BRC #48528** d12 May 22, 1989         Suki Lee*    Added code to go around a potential AppleTalk PAP bug where the system will hang trying*    to open a connection with a printer that is offline. The printer's status is now checked*    before making any PAP calls. BRC #47477 revisited***    May 25, 1989          Suki Lee*    Fixed a cut and paste error in PrPicfile where the wrong offset to the print record is *    used.**    June 2, 1989	       Suki Lee*    Added code to pass the newly added ClosePicture error to the application.**    June 5, 1989	       Suki Lee*    Added initialization of variable ZeroPage and SCBValue in PrOpenDoc as well, since some *    apps do not call anything else before the print loop. **    June 14, 1989         Mensch and Steve Glass *    We think that the low level print drivers can not handle having a band buffer that is not*    a multiple of 8 rows. We feel this is the case because of the way the printer creates empty *    lines for the end of a band. When the height of the band is being calculated, the low 3 bits*    are masked off the ensure a multiple of 8.**-------------------------------------------------------------------------------* Version 3.1* d1 December 15, 1989     Suki Lee*    AppleWorks GS had problems with printing a multipage document to an AppleTalked*    ImageWriter. The job would hang, but not always at the same page of the job. Tim*    Harrington helped narrow it down to an old bug in the AppleTalk Option Card. The*    card throws away data that is not picked up by the receiver after a given amount *    of time. Since AppleWorks GS prints each page as a job, it ran into this timing *    problem. Added code in LLDStartUp to issue an async read and code in CheckPrinter*    to retrieve data read. Also had to add provisions for direct connecting since the*    printer and modem port drivers does nothing for an async read call.** d2 January 3, 1990       Ben Koning*    Added capability to allow mid-document imaging color table changes by listening for*    a special type of PicComment while playing back the picture(s).  Also changed certain*    label and macro names to stay compatible with the ever changing include files.*    The format of the PicComment (should be done by app while recording picture) is:**	PicComment Type=251*	   word         version         0*	   word         signature       $A55A*	   word         colortableno    0..15*	   word [16]    colortable*	   long         reserved** d3 January 25, 1990      Ben Koning*    Fixed command-period bug #59501 (hitting command-period right after OK in job dialog crash).*    PrDevClose was being called without PrDevOpen having been called.  Fixed/kludged by having a*    flag called "IProcAbortEnable" to disable command-period action in the default idleproc until*    LLDStartUp has returned successfully.**    Added a "fix" for busy flag bug #55874 by calling DecBusyFlag in PrPicFile if Draft Mode.*    CDAs should now work after printing in draft mode for apps which don't use event manager.** d4 February 6, 1990      Ben Koning      Yet another KLUDGE*    Added a "fix" for case in MultiScribeGS/"MegaFonts" in Better+Condensed where the green text*    "Some Observations" would stutter vertically.  "Fixed" by commenting out two lines in the*    MakeBuff routine in the low-level driver which are intended to save time by bypassing the*    imaging algorithm output buffer in some cases.  This should add about 100 msec of time to*    each head scan, causing an 8.5x11" page to print perhaps about 4 sec slower.*************************************************************************************************************************************	 Copyright 1986-1989*	 Apple Computer, Inc.*	 All Rights Reserved*******************************************************************               Absaddr on*               Keep   IW;               MCOPY  iw.macros	Print off	include 'all.macros'	include 'iw.macros'	Print on;------------------------------------------------------------;; Global Equates;US	EQU 0FR	EQU 1Pays	EQU USVersionNb	EQU $0300	; Version 3.0;------------------------------------------------------------;; error codes;PortNotOn	EQU $1302NoPrintRecord	EQU $1303PntrConFailed	EQU $1308True	EQU $FFFFFalse	EQU $0000BTBuffSize	EQU 320	; the size we need the Quick Draw buffer to be		; for Better Text is twice the scan line width Mem64K	EQU $FFFF	; 64 K bytes of memory	ENTRY PrintDefault	;_PrDefault	ENTRY PrValidate	ENTRY PrStlDialog	ENTRY PrJobDialog	ENTRY PrDrvrVer	ENTRY PrOpenDoc	ENTRY PrCloseDoc	ENTRY PrOpenPage	ENTRY PrClosePage	ENTRY PrPicFile	ENTRY PrError	;;;;;dummy for now;;;;;;	ENTRY PrError	ENTRY PrSetError	ENTRY PrChanged	ENTRY PrPixelMap	ENTRY PrPixelMap	;;;;;dummy for now;;;;;;;	ENTRY PrGetPgOrientation	ENTRY PrGetPrinterSpecs	ENTRY LLDBitMap	ENTRY LLDSetPenPos	ENTRY LLDText	ENTRY LLDBitMap	ENTRY LLDSetPenPos	ENTRY LLDText	ENTRY LLDShutDown	ENTRY LLDSetQuality	ENTRY LLDSetColor	ENTRY LLDStartup	ENTRY LLDSetPageRect	ENTRY LLDSetMode	ENTRY Print_Test	ENTRY OpenInfoPrepare	ENTRY OurGetHandle	ENTRY StartLLD	ENTRY CloseInfo	ENTRY NewPage	ENTRY JobFilter	ENTRY StyleDialog	ENTRY JobDialog	ENTRY StyleFilter	ENTRY PrPrintIt	ENTRY PrAbortCheck	ENTRY CallIdleProc	ENTRY LLDIdleProc	ENTRY InsertPaperAlert	ENTRY NoShowMessage	ENTRY GetStatus	ENTRY PStatus	ENTRY iPrErr	IMPORT INFORECT	IMPORT ALERTTEMP320	IMPORT ALERTTEMP640	IMPORT EVTMODS	IMPORT INFOSTRBUFFER	IMPORT ERASEINFORECT	IMPORT PRINTPROCESS	IMPORT INFODPORT	IMPORT INFOSTRDRAFT	IMPORT INFOSTRPREP	IMPORT INFOSTRPOS	IMPORT INFOPORT	IMPORT INFOWINDOW	IMPORT INFORECT320	IMPORT INFORECT640	IMPORT INFOWIDTH320	IMPORT INFOWIDTH640	IMPORT EVTWHERE	IMPORT PTRLIST	IMPORT PP_LANDSC	IMPORT PP_PORTRAIT	IMPORT ASTRNUM	IMPORT JDRB0	IMPORT ASTRLIST	IMPORT ARECTLIST	IMPORT CANCELSTR	IMPORT CANCELRECT	IMPORT OKSTR	IMPORT OKRECT	IMPORT ISTRLIST	IMPORT IPOSLIST	IMPORT ISTRNUM	IMPORT PIXELWIDTH	IMPORT JISTRLIST	IMPORT JIPOSLIST	IMPORT JISTRNUM	IMPORT DSTBITF2	IMPORT DSTBITR2	IMPORT DSTBITF1	IMPORT DSTBITR1	IMPORT LANDSC_R	IMPORT PORTRAIT_R	IMPORT PIXEL320	IMPORT PIXEL640	IMPORT PORTRAIT_P	IMPORT LANDSC_P	IMPORT EVTMSG	IMPORT EVTWHAT	IMPORT IWEVENTRECORD	IMPORT IFCANCELLED	IMPORT TOFINALVALUE	IMPORT FROMFINALVALUE	IMPORT COPIEFINALVALUE	IMPORT J1STRLIST	IMPORT J1STRNUM	IMPORT SLASHSTR	IMPORT NAMEPOS	IMPORT L2	IMPORT L1	IMPORT JDRB10	IMPORT JDRBO	IMPORT JOBDTEMPLATE	IMPORT STYLEWIDTH	IMPORT STYLERECT	IMPORT SCBVALUE	IMPORT BUTTONSTATE	IMPORT JIPosList	IMPORT CoverOpenStr	IMPORT OffLineStr	IMPORT PaperJamStr	IMPORT PaperOutStr;------------------------------------------------------------------------------;------------------------------------------------------------------------------;;; Vector to appropriate printer driver routine based on value passed in X-Reg.;;;------------------------------------------------------------------------------;------------------------------------------------------------------------------IWD	PROC;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Header to denote new calls supported;	DC.W 0	; marker	DC.W (EndPrProcList-PrProcList)/4 ; count of calls supported	jmp (PrProcList,x)	;Vector to correct routinePrProcList	DC.L PrintDefault	;_PrDefault	DC.L PrValidate	DC.L PrStlDialog	DC.L PrJobDialog	DC.L PrDrvrVer	DC.L PrOpenDoc	DC.L PrCloseDoc	DC.L PrOpenPage	DC.L PrClosePage	DC.L PrPicFile	DC.L PrError	;;;;;dummy for now;;;;;;	DC.L PrError	DC.L PrSetError	DC.L PrChanged	DC.L PrPixelMap		; begin new calls	DC.L PrGetPrinterSpecs	DC.L PrGetPgOrientationEndPrProcListInvalidPr	rtl	ENDP	include 'e16.dialog'	include 'LLD.ASM'	include 'HLD.ASM'	END